{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the parameter prior sampling statements so that `rho`, `alpha`, `a`, and `eta` are each sampled exactly once before they are used to construct the Gaussian-process covariance and latent function. This preserves the same posterior density because the Stan model block log-density contributions are additive. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"// Fit the hyperparameters of a latent-variable Gaussian process with an
// exponentiated quadratic kernel and a Poisson likelihood

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real x;
  array[N] int<lower=0> y;
}
transformed data {
  real delta = 1e-9;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real a;
  vector[N] eta;
}
model {
  vector[N] f;

  rho ~ inv_gamma(5, 5);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  a ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta ~ normal(0, 1);

  {
    matrix[N, N] L_K;
    matrix[N, N] K = gp_exp_quad_cov(x, alpha, rho);

    // diagonal elements
    for (n in 1 : N) {
      K[n, n] = K[n, n] + delta;
    }

    L_K = cholesky_decompose(K);
    f = L_K * eta;
  }

  y ~ poisson_log(a + f);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":5,"x":[3.420576691812567,5.114022731447653,4.049133957156945,4.785791139561434,4.628591313590204],"y":[2,2,3,4,3]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
